<title>NETHERLANDS: Yen must not become local currency - Hashimoto.</title>
<headline>Yen must not become local currency - Hashimoto.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto said on Wednesday the yen must not be downgraded to a purely local currency.</p>
<p>&quot;The yen has no wish to be relegated to a local currency,&quot; Hashimoto told a news conference after the EU-Japan summit meeting in The Hague.  </p>
<p>A joint communique released after the summit, said a reduction in Japan's external surplus would help reduce trade tensions.</p>
<p>Hashimoto told the news conference he did not expect Japan's trade surplus with the rest of the world to rise significantly in the medium term.</p>
</text>
